msgstr "हर चैट पर Host दिखाएं"

#. Settings page and Ctrl+K, a setting's name, the row label (a switch). What it does: Show waiting messages strip above composer.
msgid "Show the queue"
msgstr "कतार दिखाएं"

#. Settings page and Ctrl+K, the line under the preference “Timestamps” saying what it does.
msgid "Show the time under each message"
msgstr "हर मैसेज के नीचे समय दिखाएं"

#. Settings page and Ctrl+K, the line under the setting “Show the queue” saying what it does
msgid "Show waiting messages strip above composer."
msgstr "मैसेज बॉक्स के ऊपर इंतज़ार कर रहे मैसेज की पट्टी दिखाएं।"

#. Settings page and Ctrl+K, a setting's name, the row label (a switch). What it does: Show replies once complete.
#. Settings page and Ctrl+K, a preference's name, the row label. What it does: Show an answer once it is complete instead of as it streams
msgid "Show when ready"
msgstr "तैयार होने पर दिखाएं"

#. chat, accessibility label of a reply's work icon (an action): shows the tool calls and steps of the turn
#. Ctrl+K command palette, a command's name (an action; a verb phrase is a command, a noun phrase names what it opens). What it does: Opens or folds the work of a finished turn in Conversation view (the message the keyboard is on, else the latest turn), or the running turn's Running box.
#. Keys (key context “Chat”): the name of a key's action, in the shortcut bar, Keys help (?) and the key-binding editor. It opens or folds the work of a finished turn in Conversation view (the message the keyboard is on, else the latest turn), or the running turn's Running box.
